WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.720 --> 00:00:02.789
In the fall of 2019, a subway

00:00:02.790 --> 00:00:04.649
fare hike in Santiago, Chile set off

00:00:04.650 --> 00:00:06.419
some of the most violent protests in

00:00:06.420 --> 00:00:08.339
Latin America's recent history.

00:00:08.340 --> 00:00:09.659
In what the media dubbed the social

00:00:09.660 --> 00:00:11.429
outburst, rioters destroyed

00:00:11.430 --> 00:00:12.989
churches, metro stations and

00:00:12.990 --> 00:00:13.859
tollbooths.

00:00:13.860 --> 00:00:15.179
The protests culminated in the

00:00:15.180 --> 00:00:17.009
election of the 36 year old leftist

00:00:17.010 --> 00:00:18.719
president Gabriel Boric, who has

00:00:18.720 --> 00:00:20.069
pledged to nationalize Chile's

00:00:20.070 --> 00:00:22.409
private pension system, raise taxes

00:00:22.410 --> 00:00:24.479
and create a more green economy.

00:00:24.480 --> 00:00:26.339
Even before that, protesters went

00:00:26.340 --> 00:00:27.689
after the Chilean constitution

00:00:27.690 --> 00:00:29.999
itself in a nationwide referendum

00:00:30.000 --> 00:00:32.669
held in October 2020, 78%

00:00:32.670 --> 00:00:34.649
of voters opted to replace it.

00:00:34.650 --> 00:00:35.639
On September 4th.

00:00:35.640 --> 00:00:36.779
They'll return to the polls to

00:00:36.780 --> 00:00:38.219
approve or reject a new draft

00:00:38.220 --> 00:00:40.439
constitution which, if passed,

00:00:40.440 --> 00:00:42.029
could bring a tragic and decisive

00:00:42.030 --> 00:00:43.739
end to Chile's so-called economic

00:00:43.740 --> 00:00:45.599
miracle that turned the country into

00:00:45.600 --> 00:00:47.459
a model for how free market policies

00:00:47.460 --> 00:00:49.289
can benefit the poor.

00:00:49.290 --> 00:00:50.879
The current constitution was adopted

00:00:50.880 --> 00:00:52.739
in 1980, when Chile was still one

00:00:52.740 --> 00:00:54.029
of Latin America's poorest

00:00:54.030 --> 00:00:54.989
countries.

00:00:54.990 --> 00:00:56.249
Over the next 40 years, the

00:00:56.250 --> 00:00:57.599
government tamed inflation,

00:00:57.600 --> 00:00:59.729
privatized industries and slashed

00:00:59.730 --> 00:01:01.889
tariffs and red tape, which caused

00:01:01.890 --> 00:01:03.839
its GDP to soar and poverty

00:01:03.840 --> 00:01:04.829
to plummet.

00:01:04.830 --> 00:01:06.899
Staples of modern living like TVs,

00:01:06.900 --> 00:01:08.789
refrigerators and washing machines

00:01:08.790 --> 00:01:10.469
became a feature in almost every

00:01:10.470 --> 00:01:11.369
home.

00:01:11.370 --> 00:01:13.409
Here's the problem, Chile's 1980

00:01:13.410 --> 00:01:15.089
constitution was adopted during the

00:01:15.090 --> 00:01:17.009
military dictatorship led by General

00:01:17.010 --> 00:01:18.839
Augusto Pinochet, who took control

00:01:18.840 --> 00:01:19.767
of the country in a murderous 1973

00:01:19.768 --> 00:01:20.768
coup.

00:01:21.930 --> 00:01:23.489
Because of this, some say the

00:01:23.490 --> 00:01:25.199
Constitution is illegitimate.

00:01:25.200 --> 00:01:26.669
The best way to address problems

00:01:26.670 --> 00:01:28.289
with the document is not to scrap it

00:01:28.290 --> 00:01:30.209
altogether, but to revise it,

00:01:30.210 --> 00:01:32.129
which is exactly what's happened.

00:01:32.130 --> 00:01:33.509
Since a return to democratic

00:01:33.510 --> 00:01:35.639
governance in 1989, the Chilean

00:01:35.640 --> 00:01:37.889
constitution has been amended 140

00:01:37.890 --> 00:01:38.969
times.

00:01:38.970 --> 00:01:40.499
Rewriting the constitution as an

00:01:40.500 --> 00:01:41.879
elected body has been doing over the

00:01:41.880 --> 00:01:44.069
past year has predictably created

00:01:44.070 --> 00:01:45.689
a feeding frenzy for political

00:01:45.690 --> 00:01:47.789
interests looking to codify special

00:01:47.790 --> 00:01:49.379
rights and privileges into the

00:01:49.380 --> 00:01:50.699
nation's most important legal

00:01:50.700 --> 00:01:51.869
document.

00:01:51.870 --> 00:01:53.279
The Economist describes the

00:01:53.280 --> 00:01:55.019
country's draft constitution as a

00:01:55.020 --> 00:01:56.909
fiscally irresponsible left wing

00:01:56.910 --> 00:01:58.079
wish list.

00:01:58.080 --> 00:02:00.119
It bans job insecurity, expands

00:02:00.120 --> 00:02:02.189
welfare programs, mandates gender

00:02:02.190 --> 00:02:04.349
parity in all public institutions,

00:02:04.350 --> 00:02:05.999
and grants social rights that would

00:02:06.000 --> 00:02:07.469
expand the role of the state in

00:02:07.470 --> 00:02:09.779
health care, education and housing.

00:02:09.780 --> 00:02:11.339
The document permits property and

00:02:11.340 --> 00:02:13.439
asset seizures by legislative decree

00:02:13.440 --> 00:02:14.999
without compensation for rightful

00:02:15.000 --> 00:02:16.199
property owners.

00:02:16.200 --> 00:02:17.819
It constraints the mining industry,

00:02:17.820 --> 00:02:19.649
eliminates school choice and would

00:02:19.650 --> 00:02:21.779
disband the Senate, making it easier

00:02:21.780 --> 00:02:23.009
for the executive branch to

00:02:23.010 --> 00:02:24.959
circumvent the opposition and enact

00:02:24.960 --> 00:02:25.859
its agenda.

00:02:25.860 --> 00:02:27.389
These provisions are spelled out in

00:02:27.390 --> 00:02:29.399
almost 54,000 words,

00:02:29.400 --> 00:02:31.109
which is about seven times as long

00:02:31.110 --> 00:02:32.609
as the US Constitution.

00:02:32.610 --> 00:02:34.199
Unlike that document, which has been

00:02:34.200 --> 00:02:36.059
in place since 1788,

00:02:36.060 --> 00:02:37.499
the Chilean draft constitution

00:02:37.500 --> 00:02:39.599
focuses on expanding state power

00:02:39.600 --> 00:02:41.609
rather than constraining it.

00:02:41.610 --> 00:02:43.499
Chile's draft constitution is even

00:02:43.500 --> 00:02:45.359
longer than Venezuela's, which

00:02:45.360 --> 00:02:47.009
was redrafted by Hugo Chavez's

00:02:47.010 --> 00:02:48.809
administration during his first year

00:02:48.810 --> 00:02:50.669
in office and set the stage

00:02:50.670 --> 00:02:51.749
for the country's socialist

00:02:51.750 --> 00:02:53.219
revolution, descent into

00:02:53.220 --> 00:02:55.229
dictatorship and ensuing economic

00:02:55.230 --> 00:02:56.639
collapse.

00:02:56.640 --> 00:02:59.189
Venezuela has had 26 constitutions

00:02:59.190 --> 00:03:01.259
in a little over two centuries.

00:03:01.260 --> 00:03:02.579
In general, the practice of

00:03:02.580 --> 00:03:03.869
scrapping and rewriting

00:03:03.870 --> 00:03:05.879
constitutions helps to explain

00:03:05.880 --> 00:03:07.769
Latin America's relentless political

00:03:07.770 --> 00:03:08.879
turmoil.

00:03:08.880 --> 00:03:10.439
The constitution provides legal

00:03:10.440 --> 00:03:12.449
stability and predictability, like

00:03:12.450 --> 00:03:14.429
a computer operating system.

00:03:14.430 --> 00:03:16.199
Tampering with any foundational code

00:03:16.200 --> 00:03:17.939
create security holes that are

00:03:17.940 --> 00:03:19.499
easily exploited by political

00:03:19.500 --> 00:03:21.629
opportunists looking to amplify

00:03:21.630 --> 00:03:23.249
their own power and overturn the

00:03:23.250 --> 00:03:24.809
established order.

00:03:24.810 --> 00:03:26.249
Even if Chileans reject the new

00:03:26.250 --> 00:03:28.169
constitution, and thankfully polls

00:03:28.170 --> 00:03:30.059
indicate that they probably will,

00:03:30.060 --> 00:03:31.259
Boric can choose to start the

00:03:31.260 --> 00:03:32.789
process again with the election of

00:03:32.790 --> 00:03:34.829
yet another constitutional assembly

00:03:34.830 --> 00:03:36.779
to draft yet another version that

00:03:36.780 --> 00:03:38.819
could bring years of chaos, economic

00:03:38.820 --> 00:03:41.309
stagnation and legal uncertainty.

00:03:41.310 --> 00:03:42.869
Now that Latin America's free market

00:03:42.870 --> 00:03:44.729
experiment and economic miracle is

00:03:44.730 --> 00:03:46.559
coming to an end, hopefully

00:03:46.560 --> 00:03:47.909
the rest of the world can learn from

00:03:47.910 --> 00:03:50.069
the experience of Chile once again.

00:03:50.070 --> 00:03:51.659
Beware leftist pipe dreams.

